# This repo is edited on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) but every file in it is either
# hand-written Markdown or synced byte-for-byte from mb-core, which generates LF
# unconditionally. Pin the whole repo to LF so the bytes on disk match what the
# generators produce, and so the working tree does not depend on any individual
# developer's core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a checkout on a machine with
# autocrlf unset or false rewrites the working copy to CRLF, and the next
# `openapi:sync` reports a spurious full-file diff instead of the real change.
* text=auto eol=lf

# This repo has core.autocrlf=true; the mb-core repo that GENERATES the files below
# has core.autocrlf=input. The generators
# (apps/open-api-mb/scripts/openapi.ts, apps/open-api-mb/scripts/docs-contract.ts) write LF
# unconditionally, and the sync step copies them here byte-for-byte. Without this rule,
# checkout would rewrite the working copy to CRLF, so the two repos' copies would no longer
# be byte-identical on disk and the next sync would produce a spurious full-file diff instead
# of the real change.
#
# Redundant with the blanket rule above, and kept deliberately so: these two are the
# only files whose LF-ness is load-bearing for a check, so an explicit pin should
# survive any future edit that narrows or removes the blanket rule.
api-reference/openapi.json text eol=lf
api-reference/docs-contract.json text eol=lf
